<title>GERMANY: Hesse March CPI falls 0.1 pct, rises 1.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Hesse March CPI falls 0.1 pct, rises 1.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The consumer price index for the German state of Hesse fell by 0.1 percent in March from February and rose by 1.4 percent year-on-year, the state's statistics office said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In February, the state reported an 0.3 percent month-on-month rise and a 1.5 percent year-on-year rise.</p>
<p>Date for four west German states are used to calculate a preliminary figure for Germany as a whole.</p>
<p>The statistics office gave the following breakdown of its Hesse cost of living data :</p>
<p>						 Percentage change</p>
<p> Index/component			   mth/mth   yr/yr    Index</p>
<p> Overall price index		     -0.1	+1.4     115.1</p>
<p> Prices exc heating oil, fuel	  -0.1	+1.2     115.0</p>
<p> Prices exc seasonal goods	     -0.1	+1.5     115.5</p>
<p> Rents					 +0.1	+2.8     128.0</p>
<p> Household energy			  -1.5	+2.8     100.0</p>
<p> Personal goods, services and other  -0.9	+2.5     124.0</p>
<p> Transport and communications	  +0.2	+0.4     114.9</p>
<p> Furniture and other household goods unch	+0.5     111.3</p>
<p> Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	   -0.2	+0.2     109.9</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes			   unch	+0.7     108.7</p>
<p> Health and personal care items	+0.1	+1.3     112.2</p>
<p> Education, entertainment, leisure   unch	+2.2     113.4</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
